{"parentUuid":"092ab334-6ce0-4f7d-af52-d17ad4dbfb11","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a5742d151ebfb6c56","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CffuWMk4HQpgnGV1Mi2Gi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014z25Qvssegj14qH4WJJDqn","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-nsviridenko-ws-sloprail-harness-mocks--claude-worktrees-harness-mocks-architecture-3031e7/f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666/scratchpad/brief.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5510,"cache_read_input_tokens":45048,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5510,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":21,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_014z25Qvssegj14qH4WJJDqn":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-nsviridenko-ws-sloprail-harness-mocks--claude-worktrees-harness-mocks-architecture-3031e7/f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666/scratchpad/brief.md"}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CffuWMSSsfy8WtRsPurRe","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"fbba2b25-6e19-446b-bac4-3ac549f02651","timestamp":"2026-10-03T20:06:34.722Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a5742d151ebfb6c56","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-aefdb38925cd179a2"}
{"parentUuid":"fbba2b25-6e19-446b-bac4-3ac549f02651","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"a5742d151ebfb6c56","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014z25Qvssegj14qH4WJJDqn","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tYou are one of 31 parallel agents; each takes ONE capability in the repo you are in (a git worktree of sloprail/harness-mocks). Goal: every `pending` cell of your capability's spec file (spec/capabilities/<id>.yaml) becomes real: **supported** (docs + recorded runs of the REAL harness, an adapter in the mock, tests) or **unsupported with evidence**. Recorded runs outrank docs: a run showing the behaviour (even partly) => supported, the gaps listed as `deviations`; a run showing the behaviour absent (whose scenario really attempts it) => `{supported: false, reason: <one line>, runs: [...] and/or docs: [...]}`. Never leave `pending`, never a bare `false`. Do NOT change the capability's `statement` (that needs the user's words) nor other capabilities' cells.\n2\t\n3\tA finished example, already on main: `git show f860ff3` (codex x bash-tool-result): scenario under codex-mock/snapshots/runs/<name>/setup/, captured with the harness's snapshots/capture.sh, cell in the spec file, `// sr:provides <id>/<harness>` adapter marker, `// sr:proves <id>/<harness>` test. Read it first, plus adr/capability-grounding, adr/capability-once, adr/modeled-surface, .sloprail/schemas/capability.cue, and the existing cells and tests of the same harness.\n4\t\n5\tHow things work\n6\t- Real harnesses are installed and logged in: `codex` and `cursor-agent`. Record with `<harness>-mock/snapshots/capture.sh run <name>` (the ONLY writer of snapshots/; hand-authored `setup/` = prompt.txt, hooks.json, hook scripts, optional args/env; read the script's header and the existing runs). It makes real model calls: keep prompts short, and capture only what you need (a few runs). Captures are serialised by a lock per harness; wait for it. `capture.sh doc <url>` freezes a doc page into the MANIFEST (cells cite `https://...#anchor` of a frozen page). Reuse existing runs when they already show the behaviour (cite them), else add new ones; run names are kebab-case; a new run name you create must be unique to your capability (prefix it with the capability id or a clear name) so parallel agents don't collide.\n7\t- Look at what the real harness did (events.jsonl, stream.jsonl, payloads.jsonl, transcript/) before deciding. Your own scenario must really attempt the behaviour; if the harness cannot do it (no such tool/hook/flag), record the attempt and mark the cell unsupported citing that run (and docs if they show it).\n8\t- Supported cell: the mock's adapter (<harness>-mock/) provides it, core behaviour lives once in internal/ (`// sr:capability <id>` already exists there; behaviour that differs per harness is a PARAMETER of core, never a copy). An adapter translates and decides nothing. Mark adapter code `// sr:provides <id>/<harness>`, and add e2e/unit tests marked `// sr:proves <id>/<harness>` (on tests only, in *_test.go) that replay/drive the mock into the recorded situation and assert what the recording shows (or the declared deviation). Unsupported cells have NO markers. `deviations` are `{adr, statement}`: use `adr: modeled-surface` where the mock models less than the harness does (interactive-only things, unimplemented tools/events), and `adr: capability-grounding` where the real harness itself doesn't do a part of the statement.\n9\t- Scope: if modelling the behaviour in the mock is large, model what the recordings show of it and declare the rest as modeled-surface deviations; do not fake behaviour the recordings don't show.\n10\t- CRITICAL for judges: the rules judge every capability that has a marker in any file you touch (whole file). So do NOT edit existing files that carry other capabilities' markers unless unavoidable; prefer NEW files for your adapter code and tests (new Go files must lie in a module home: see the module.yaml files / adr/modules-cover-code; internal/ and *-mock/ code each belongs to exactly one module). If you must touch a file with other markers, expect the judges to also re-judge those pairs and be ready to satisfy them. Keep `file-size` and `layering` ADR limits. Other agents work in parallel on other capabilities; touch only what yours needs; shared core edits should be small, additive, parameterised.\n11\t- Verify: `go build ./... && go vet ./...`, tests of what you touched (`go test -count=1 ./<harness>-mock/... ./internal/... ./tools/...`; e2e suites build the mock themselves), gofmt. Then commit (signed commits are on; message body ends with `Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>`), `git fetch origin && git rebase origin/main` (conflicts, e.g. MANIFEST.yaml, are plain merges: keep both sides; if a rebase changes snapshot files, never hand-edit sealed samples), then run the repo's checks: `sr-checks run --base origin/main --head HEAD` (runs judges with a model, ~1-3 min; it caches by content; repeat until it prints no refusals). Read each refusal and fix the cause (a test that doesn't assert what the recording shows, a deviation that is false, a cell not shown by its citations...). A refusal about something clearly pre-existing and unrelated to your change: report it rather than rewriting other capabilities.\n12\t- Merge: `git push -u origin HEAD`, `gh pr create --base main` (title \"<harness>: <id> ...\"; body ends with \"🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\"), wait for CI (`gh pr checks <n> --watch`), and when ALL checks pass: `gh pr merge <n> --squash --admin` (the user authorised admin-merge when CI passes). If main moved meanwhile and CI/verify fails on a stale base, rebase, re-run sr-checks, push --force-with-lease, and retry. Never merge with a failing check.\n13\t- Do not touch other worktrees, never use bare `git stash`, never `cd` out of your worktree.\n14\t\n15\tFinal report (short): per cell: supported/unsupported, runs captured, what you implemented, PR number and merge status, anything left red and why.\n16\t\n17\tCapture gotcha (cursor): the installed `cursor-agent` may be newer (2026.10.01) than snapshots/MANIFEST.yaml's version (2026.09.28), and capture.sh refuses. Do NOT run `capture.sh all`. Instead put the 2026.09.28 build on PATH for the capture: look in `~/.local/share/cursor-agent/versions/` for the directory of that version and prepend it to PATH (`PATH=<dir>:$PATH cursor-mock/snapshots/capture.sh run <name>`; check `cursor-agent --version` prints 2026.09.28 first).\n18\t"}]},"uuid":"5d21334f-bd28-40b7-bced-395b840e5ee2","timestamp":"2026-10-03T20:06:35.085Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"fbba2b25-6e19-446b-bac4-3ac549f02651","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a5742d151ebfb6c56","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-aefdb38925cd179a2"}
{"parentUuid":"5d21334f-bd28-40b7-bced-395b840e5ee2","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a5742d151ebfb6c56","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CffuWMk4HQpgnGV1Mi2Gi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01L9ytyY5xyB33TSvvGajwae","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git status | head -3 && ls && cat spec/capabilities/session-start-hook.yaml | head -150 && ls codex-mock/snapshots/runs | grep -E \"session-start|manual-compaction\""},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5510,"cache_read_input_tokens":45048,"output_tokens":312,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5510},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":312,"cache_read_input_tokens":45048,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5510,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5510,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01L9ytyY5xyB33TSvvGajwae":{"command":"cd /Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a5742d151ebfb6c56 && git status | head -3 && ls && cat spec/capabilities/session-start-hook.yaml | head -150 && ls codex-mock/snapshots/runs | grep -E \"session-start|manual-compaction\""}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01L9ytyY5xyB33TSvvGajwae":{"cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a5742d151ebfb6c56"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CffuWMSSsfy8WtRsPurRe","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"49ed681f-6b12-4397-953d-426e6ee15402","timestamp":"2026-10-03T20:06:35.378Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a5742d151ebfb6c56","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-aefdb38925cd179a2"}
{"parentUuid":"49ed681f-6b12-4397-953d-426e6ee15402","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"a5742d151ebfb6c56","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L9ytyY5xyB33TSvvGajwae","type":"tool_result","content":"On branch worktree-agent-a5742d151ebfb6c56\nnothing to commit, working tree clean\nCLA.md\nCONTRIBUTING.md\nLICENSE\nREADME.md\nadr\nclaude-mock\ncodex-mock\ncursor-mock\ngo.mod\ngo.sum\ninternal\nproposals\nspec\ntools\nstatement: >-\n  A hook fires when a session begins and, in a harness that starts a session\n  in more than one way, says how it began: fresh, resumed, forked, or\n  continuing after a compaction. The hook cannot stop the session from\n  starting. (What else the hook receives or may return, such as context for\n  the agent, is other capabilities'.)\nproviders:\n  claude:\n    docs:\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#sessionstart-input\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#sessionstart-decision-control\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#exit-code-2-behavior-per-event\n    runs:\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/hookerrors\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/stops\n    deviations:\n      - adr: modeled-surface\n        statement: >-\n          A session cleared with /clear starts again with source \"clear\" in\n          Claude Code. The mock parses no slash command, so it never reports\n          that source.\n  codex:\n    docs:\n      - https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks#sessionstart\n    runs:\n      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/stops\n      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-exit-codes\n      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-matchers\n      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/session-start-continue-false\n    deviations:\n      - adr: modeled-surface\n        statement: >-\n          The mock never resumes, forks or compacts a session, so a session start is always the fresh one, source startup.\n  cursor:\n    docs:\n      - https://cursor.com/docs/hooks#sessionstart\n    runs:\n      - cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/session-start-block\n      - cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/session-start-continue-false\n      - cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/symlinked-cwd\n    deviations:\n      - adr: modeled-surface\n        statement: >-\n          The mock never resumes, forks or compacts a conversation, so it fires\n          one sessionStart hook per run, at the fresh start.\nmanual-compaction-auto\nmanual-compaction-auto-blocked\nmanual-compaction-auto-post-stopped\nmanual-compaction-slash\nsession-start-continue-false","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"badd5110-c560-4a87-833e-d1b25a476505","timestamp":"2026-10-03T20:06:35.842Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"49ed681f-6b12-4397-953d-426e6ee15402","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a5742d151ebfb6c56","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-aefdb38925cd179a2"}
