{"parentUuid":"93373f06-897b-4ecc-840a-6dd403972a8a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"a5742d151ebfb6c56","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CCpLkttP7GyL6G5nKDzE1E","type":"tool_result","content":"          Claude Code. The mock parses no slash command, so it never reports\n          that source.\n  codex:\n    docs:\n      - https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks#sessionstart\n    runs:\n      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/stops\n      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-exit-codes\n      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-matchers\n      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/session-start-continue-false\n      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/session-start-compact-continue-false\n      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto\n    deviations:\n      - adr: modeled-surface\n        statement: >-\n<<<<<<< HEAD\n          The mock never forks, compacts or clears a session (the sources clear and compact), so a session start is the fresh one, source startup, or the one a session resumed by its id (`exec resume`) makes, source resume.\n      - adr: capability-grounding\n        statement: >-\n          Unlike the statement, a Codex SessionStart hook can stop the run: one\n          returning {\"continue\":false} ends it at once, with no prompt hook,\n          tool call or model request after it (recorded:\n          runs/session-start-continue-false).\n=======\n          The mock never resumes or forks a session, so its session starts are\n          the fresh one (source startup) and the one after a compaction (source\n          compact).\n>>>>>>> 600c1ad8 (codex: a compact session start's continue:false ends the turn, recorded and replayed (session-start-hook))\n  cursor:\n    docs:\n      - https://cursor.com/docs/hooks#sessionstart\n    runs:\n      - cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/session-start-block\n      - cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/session-start-continue-false\n      - cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/symlinked-cwd\n    deviations:\n      - adr: modeled-surface\n        statement: >-\n          The mock never forks or compacts a conversation, so it fires one\n          sessionStart hook per run, at the fresh start.\n      - adr: capability-grounding\n        statement: >-\n          A conversation resumed by its id (`--resume`) fires no sessionStart\n          hook in cursor-agent, and the mock does the same\n          (recorded: runs/session-resume).","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"78b9f836-4cdf-4a2c-9f2e-c97500268519","timestamp":"2026-10-03T20:16:02.690Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"93373f06-897b-4ecc-840a-6dd403972a8a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a5742d151ebfb6c56","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-aefdb38925cd179a2"}
